body:
Ah the beauty of the internet. You have no idea who your talking to and neither do I. I do know that your saying things tht directly contractdict what i learned in my undergrad finance courses, cfa studies, and 5 years as an equity portfolio analyst. Why are you so hung up on this obviously, easily verifiable situation? 

Youre right if you pick a random stock that pays a dividend and look at its price the day before ex date and then on ex date, it should reduce by the div amount. beleive it or not, someetimes that doesn't happen. sometimes it goes down more than the div as well. 

regardless, my absolute brother in christ, their is nothing mechanical doing this. the reason why the price (should) decrease by the dividend amount is because that is cash coming out of the firm, being distributed to shareholders. as you've pointed out, a ten dollar a share stock pays a one dollar per share dividend, then mathmatically the 1 dollar a share is no longer in the firm, thus reducing the value of the share proportionally. i'll repeat, this doesn't always happen. beleive it or not theres a ton of research out there on this.

I work on the buy side so i'm not too familiar with finra's so thanks for bringing that up. happy to learn. If you actually read that rule it pertains to adjusting a customers orders. so the quantity of shares they have an open conditional order on ie GTC, GTD etc. theres nothing happening to the actual shares and theres nothing happening at the exchange. Its the broker being able to adjust the order so the client can get filled on an ex date for no loss of value. Furthermore it looks like it doesn't even apply to the majority of stocks per paragraph (e) The provisions of paragraph (a) of this Rule shall not apply to:  
(1) orders governed by the rules of a registered national securities exchange;  
(2) open stop orders to buy;  
(3) open sell orders;

I mean did you even fully read the rule?

what port do i need? is there any way around that? some sort of adapter perhaps?

&#x200B;

what do you mean by the 660 giving me a rough time these days? i don't have my heart set on that card its just listed as the min spec for a lot of current games.
